edia/empire-of-japan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/empire-of-japan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Empire of Japan</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Empire of Japan was the Japanese state from the Meiji Restoration of 1868 until the post-war constitution of 1947.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/empire-on-which-the-sun-never-sets"><span class="enc-name">Empire on which the sun never sets</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">The 'empire on which the sun never sets' is a phrase describing an empire so extensive that some part of it is always in daylight.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/emporda"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emporda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Empordà</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Empordà is a region of north-eastern Catalonia in Spain, between the Pyrenees and the Mediterranean, now divided into Alt Empordà and Baix Empordà.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/emporio-chios"><span class="enc-name">Emporio (Chios)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Emporio is a harbour site on the south coast of Chios in Greece, excavated by the British School at Athens in the 1950s.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/empress-dowager-bo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/empress-dowager-bo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Empress Dowager Bo</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Empress Dowager Bo, born Bo Ji, was a consort of Liu Bang, founder of the Han dynasty, and the mother of Emperor Wen.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/empress-dowager-cixi"><img class="enc